# GSAP

GSAP is 100% free as of 2025, including SplitText, ScrollSmoother, MorphSVG, and DrawSVG. No Club membership, no plugin gating. Import them directly.

## The core conflict
Animations fail when CSS sets `opacity: 0`, `visibility: hidden`, or `display: none` and GSAP fights it — or when GSAP sets an initial state that CSS then overrides.

**GSAP controls visibility, not CSS.** If GSAP animates opacity or visibility on an element, remove every CSS rule touching those properties on it.

```tsx
// correct
gsap.set('.element', { opacity: 0, y: 20 })
gsap.to('.element', { opacity: 1, y: 0 })

// wrong — CSS fights GSAP
// .element { opacity: 0; }
```

## Tailwind classes to strip
`invisible`, `hidden`, `opacity-0` on any element GSAP will animate. Let `gsap.set()` establish the initial state instead.

## ScrollTrigger
```tsx
ScrollTrigger.create({
  trigger: '.element',
  onEnter: () => gsap.to('.element', { opacity: 1 }),
})
```
The element must exist in DOM flow. `display: none` breaks trigger detection. Parent containers must be visible.

Call `ScrollTrigger.refresh()` after any layout change — font load, image load, route transition.

## Debugging
```tsx
const el = document.querySelector('.element')
console.log(getComputedStyle(el).opacity, getComputedStyle(el).visibility, getComputedStyle(el).display)
```

## React
Use `useGSAP()` from `@gsap/react` for automatic cleanup. Scope selectors to a ref container so animations don't leak across components. Register plugins once: `gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger)`.

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — gate or shorten animations, don't ship motion that can't be turned off.

## Before animating
- [ ] No CSS opacity/visibility on animated elements
- [ ] No Tailwind `hidden`, `invisible`, `opacity-0`
- [ ] `gsap.set()` used for initial states
- [ ] Parent containers visible
- [ ] ScrollTrigger elements in DOM flow
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` handled
